  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile with avgpool aggregation (config_002, acc=0.512) substantially outperforms singleprofile with no aggregation (config_051, acc=0.427), an ~8.5-point gap. This tells us that combining multiple profiles helps, but it does not tell us whether the aggregation *mechanism* matters or whether the gain is simply from having more data to average. Config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, transformer, concat) is a single-variable change from config_002, swapping only avgpool for transformer aggregation. If transformer significantly improves over avgpool, it indicates profiles carry heterogeneous information requiring structured combination, justifying further investment in aggregation design. If the gain is marginal, it confirms simple averaging is sufficient and we should redirect budget toward other axes (e.g., image encoder or fusion method). This is the most informative next step because it isolates the aggregation decision while holding all other design choices at their currently best-known values."
}

